WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.910
1 January 2021.

2
00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:07.170
In Africa, trading begins
under a new free trade area.

3
00:00:07.220 --> 00:00:10.982
The same day, the UK ends
free movement with the EU.

4
00:00:11.032 --> 00:00:15.170
EU citizens now need 70
points for a work visa.

5
00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:19.150
The stated aim was to reduce
overall migration numbers.

6
00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:26.150
UK net migration peaked at 944,000,
in the twelve months to March 2023.

7
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:29.950
So how far can governments
control global interactions?

8
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.950
Can a border simply stop the flow?

9
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.010
In this mission, you'll climb
the ladder of integration,

10
00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:39.130
from a free trade area to a single market.

11
00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:43.050
Then you'll visit Shenzhen, China's
first special economic zone,

12
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.190
and test the UK's rules against the data.

13
00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:51.200
Your mission: evaluate how far governments
can control global interactions.
